---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { img } from '../lib/images';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { clients, credentials, practice, principalBio, services, stats, team } from '../data/studio';

const schema = [
  {
    '@type': 'Person',
    '@id': `${site.url}/studio#principal`,
    name: 'Ar. Pravin Kudkar',
    jobTitle: 'Founder and principal architect',
    worksFor: { '@id': `${site.url}/#organization` },
    alumniOf: {
      '@type': 'CollegeOrUniversity',
      name: 'Kamla Raheja Vidyanidhi Institute for Architecture, Mumbai',
    },
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="About us"
  description="Wall Voids Architects is a Mumbai practice led by Ar. Pravin Kudkar, carrying projects from brief through drawings, approvals and site as one continuous act."
  path="/studio"
  active="/studio"
  footerVariant="full"
  spineId="st-spine"
  schema={schema}
>
  <span slot="header-meta">{site.localityLine}</span>
  <span slot="header-meta" style="display:block;width:26px;height:1px;background:#e2231a"></span>

  <section style="padding:112px var(--gut) 0">
    {/* See the note on /projects: display heading and standfirst removed, eyebrow promoted to h1. */}
    <div data-r="split" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.35fr .65fr;gap:56px;align-items:end">
      <h1
        style="margin:0;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;font-size:10px;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:.3em;text-transform:uppercase;white-space:nowrap;opacity:.5;animation:stUp 1s .1s cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1) both"
      >
        <span style="width:4px;height:4px;border-radius:50%;background:#e2231a"></span>About us
      </h1>
    </div>
    <div data-draw style="height:1px;background:rgba(13,13,13,.28);margin-top:34px"></div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding:56px var(--gut) 0">
    {/*
      The Gami Jaydeep Estella walkthrough takes this banner at the practice's request,
      replacing the Transindia Grandeur render, which came off the site with it.

      The band takes the film's own 16:9 instead of the 66vh it used to be. That matters:
      66vh was about 2.4:1 and the render in it was cover-cropped to fit, which is what
      the `object-position` note here used to be about. A film has no safe crop — every
      shot is framed — so the band is the film's shape and the fit is `contain`.

      Reduced motion is handled by the same code as the home page's film: both carry
      `data-autoloop`, and under `prefers-reduced-motion` they are paused and rewound so
      the poster frame shows and nothing moves.
    */}
    <figure data-plate style="margin:0">
      <div data-mask style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:16 / 9;background:#0d0d0d;border:1px solid rgba(13,13,13,.1)">
        <video
          data-autoloop
          autoplay
          loop
          muted
          playsinline
          preload="metadata"
          poster="/video/estella.jpg"
          aria-label="A walkthrough of Gami Jaydeep Estella — the street approach at dusk, the entrance porch, the balcony facade, and an aerial view of the podium at night."
          style="display:block;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:contain;background:#0d0d0d"
        >
          <source src="/video/estella.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
        </video>
      </div>
      <figcaption
        style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:24px;padding-top:13px;font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.22em;text-transform:uppercase;opacity:.45"
        data-rv
      >
        <span>Gami Jaydeep Estella — walkthrough</span><span style="white-space:nowrap">Gami Group &amp; Jaydeep Group</span>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section style="padding:120px var(--gut) 0">
    <div
      style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;gap:32px;padding-bottom:14px"
      data-rv
    >
      <div
        style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.3em;text-transform:uppercase;white-space:nowrap;opacity:.5"
      >
        <span style="width:4px;height:4px;border-radius:50%;background:#e2231a"></span>01 / Practice
      </div>
      {/*
        The margin note used to hang in the empty right half of the grid below, which is
        the half this section no longer has. It sits on the section's own header row now,
        where every other section on the site puts its right-hand note.
      */}
      <div style="font-family:Caveat,cursive;font-size:17px;line-height:1.5;color:rgba(13,13,13,.6);white-space:nowrap">
        one hand, brief to handover
      </div>
    </div>
    <div data-draw style="height:1px;background:rgba(13,13,13,.26)"></div>
    {/*
      [DESIGN CHANGE — requested] The practice asked why the type size changed partway
      through this section, and for a better use of the page.

      Both had the same cause. The first paragraph was set as a lede at clamp(17px,
      1.9vw,23px) and full opacity, the other two at body size and .66 — a device that
      works for one display sentence above a body block, but these three paragraphs are
      one continuous description of the practice, so the step read as a mistake. They
      are one setting now: same size, same leading, same opacity.

      The layout followed from that. All three sat in columns 1-7 with a 62ch cap, so
      the first paragraph ran to 790px while the other two stopped at 533px — a ragged
      right edge against an empty right half of the page. One paragraph per column
      across all twelve fills the width, gives each the same measure, and matches how
      Team, Clients and Services below already use the grid.
    */}
    {/*
      [DESIGN CHANGE — requested] Text left, plate right. The three paragraphs stack in
      columns 1-6 and the plate takes 8-12.

      Alignment, which is the part the practice asked to be careful about, took two
      things. The plate is 1500x2000 — a 3:4 portrait — so its height is set by its
      width, and the wider the screen the taller it gets: filling five columns it stood
      749px at 1512 and 976px at 1920, against a text column of about 510px either way.
      Left alone the two would have drifted further apart the bigger the screen.

      So: the stats row moves inside the left column rather than sitting in its own band
      below, which lifts that column from about 360px to about 510px; and the plate is
      capped at 480px wide and held to the right of its column, which fixes its height
      near 640px at every desktop width instead of letting it grow. The two columns
      share a top edge and now end within about 100px of each other from 1280 to 1920,
      where before the gap was 240px and rising.

      The plate keeps its own ratio under `object-fit: contain`, so it is shown whole —
      capping the width rather than the height is what makes that possible.

      `data-rv` sits on the grid rather than on each paragraph: the reveal ends at
      `opacity: 1`, so marking the paragraphs individually would override their own .72
      and set the prose solid black.
    */}
    <div
      data-r="g12"
      data-rv
      style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(12,1fr);gap:28px;padding-top:56px;align-items:start"
    >
      <div data-practicetext style="grid-column:1 / span 6">
        {practice.map((para, i) => (
          <p
            data-prose
            style={`margin:${i === 0 ? '0' : '26px 0 0'};font-size:13px;line-height:1.85;opacity:.72;text-wrap:pretty`}
          >
            {para}
          </p>
        ))}
        <div data-r="g3" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:28px;padding-top:56px">
      {
        stats.map((s) => (
          <div data-rv>
            <div style="font-size:clamp(32px,4.2vw,52px);line-height:1;font-weight:300;letter-spacing:-.03em">
              <span data-countto={String(s.value)}>0</span>
              {s.suffix}
            </div>
            <div data-draw style="height:1px;background:#e2231a;margin-top:16px" />
            <div style="margin-top:13px;font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.24em;text-transform:uppercase;opacity:.5">
              {s.label}
            </div>
          </div>
        ))
      }
        </div>
      </div>

      {/*
        Supplied by the practice 7 November 2026. No project is named for it, so the alt
        text describes what the frame shows and no caption asserts a name — the same
        footing as the Entrance Gateway plate on the contact page.
      */}
      <div
        data-practiceplate
        data-mask
        style="grid-column:8 / span 5;width:min(100%, 480px);margin-left:auto"
      >
        <Image
          src={img('img/p/towers-night.webp')}
          alt="Twin residential towers lit at dusk, with an arched entrance gateway and landscaped forecourt at their base"
          widths={[480, 760, 1100, 1500]}
          sizes="(max-width: 980px) 100vw, 480px"
          style="display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:contain"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding:120px var(--gut) 0">
    <div
      style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.3em;text-transform:uppercase;white-space:nowrap;opacity:.5;padding-bottom:14px"
      data-rv
    >
      <span style="width:4px;height:4px;border-radius:50%;background:#e2231a"></span>02 / Principal
    </div>
    <div data-draw style="height:1px;background:rgba(13,13,13,.26)"></div>
    <div
      data-r="g12"
      data-rv
      style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(12,1fr);gap:28px;padding-top:56px;align-items:start"
    >
      {/*
        [DESIGN CHANGE — requested] Same fix as the Practice section above. Everything
        here sat in columns 1-7, so the bio stopped at 533px and the right half of the
        page was empty for the whole section.

        The name now spans the grid, the three bio paragraphs take a column each at the
        same setting as Practice, and the credentials run two-up. The earlier note here
        warned that a credentials row stretched to 1200px would strand its label and its
        value at opposite ends of the screen; two columns of roughly 690px keeps each
        row the width it was while still using the page.
      */}
      <h2
        style="grid-column:1 / span 12;margin:0;font-size:clamp(22px,2.6vw,32px);line-height:1.1;font-weight:300;letter-spacing:-.02em"
      >
        Ar. Pravin Kudkar
      </h2>
      {principalBio.map((para, i) => (
        <p
          data-prose
          style={`grid-column:${1 + i * 4} / span 4;margin:26px 0 0;font-size:13px;line-height:1.85;opacity:.72;text-wrap:pretty`}
        >
          {para}
        </p>
      ))}
      <div
        data-r="credgrid"
        style="grid-column:1 / span 12;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:0 56px;margin-top:40px"
      >
        {credentials.map((c) => (
          <div
            data-r="labelrow"
            style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:150px 1fr;gap:24px;align-items:baseline;padding:19px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(13,13,13,.1)"
            data-rv
          >
            <span style="font-size:8.5px;letter-spacing:.24em;text-transform:uppercase;opacity:.42;white-space:nowrap">
              {c.label}
            </span>
            <span style="font-size:13px;line-height:1.7;opacity:.75">{c.value}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/*
    The team the practice supplied on 4 November 2026. A new section, added at its
    request, and built from parts the page already uses: the title block, the drawn
    rule, and the two-column label row the credentials above are set in. Clients and
    Services move to 04 and 05 so the numbering still reads in order.
  */}
  <section style="padding:120px var(--gut) 0">
    <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;gap:32px;padding-bottom:14px" data-rv>
      <div
        style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.3em;text-transform:uppercase;white-space:nowrap;opacity:.5"
      >
        <span style="width:4px;height:4px;border-radius:50%;background:#e2231a"></span>03 / Team
      </div>
      <div style="font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;white-space:nowrap;opacity:.5">
        {team.length} alongside the principal
      </div>
    </div>
    <div data-draw style="height:1px;background:rgba(13,13,13,.26)"></div>
    <div data-r="g2" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:0 56px;padding-top:20px">
      {
        team.map((t) => (
          <div
            style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;align-items:baseline;gap:16px;padding:19px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(13,13,13,.1)"
            data-rv
          >
            <span style="display:block;width:16px;height:1px;background:#e2231a" />
            <span>
              <span style="display:block;font-size:15px;line-height:1.4;letter-spacing:-.01em">{t.name}</span>
              <span style="display:block;margin-top:5px;font-size:9px;letter-spacing:.24em;text-transform:uppercase;opacity:.5">
                {t.role}
              </span>
              {t.note && (
                <span style="display:block;margin-top:8px;font-size:12px;line-height:1.75;opacity:.62;text-wrap:pretty">
                  {t.note}
                </span>
              )}
            </span>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding:120px var(--gut) 0">
    <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;gap:32px;padding-bottom:14px" data-rv>
      <div
        style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.3em;text-transform:uppercase;white-space:nowrap;opacity:.5"
      >
        <span style="width:4px;height:4px;border-radius:50%;background:#e2231a"></span>04 / Clients
      </div>
      <div style="font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;white-space:nowrap;opacity:.5">
        Developers worked with
      </div>
    </div>
    <div data-draw style="height:1px;background:rgba(13,13,13,.26)"></div>
    <div data-r="g4" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:10px;padding-top:40px" data-rv>
    {/*
      [BUG FIX] These tiles were `white-space: nowrap`, so each one's text set a floor
      under its grid track. With the eleventh name — "M/S Real Infrastructure Co", the
      longest in the list — four tracks no longer fitted between 981px and about 1030px,
      and the document ran up to 45px past the viewport. Letting a long name wrap lets
      the track shrink; the tiles are already centred, so a two-line name sits correctly.
    */}
      {
        clients.map((cl) => (
          <span
            data-cl
            style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;border:1px solid rgba(13,13,13,.14);padding:19px 12px;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;text-align:center;color:rgba(13,13,13,.55);transition:border-color .45s ease,color .45s ease"
          >
            {cl}
          </span>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding:120px var(--gut) 0">
    <div
      style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.3em;text-transform:uppercase;white-space:nowrap;opacity:.5;padding-bottom:14px"
      data-rv
    >
      <span style="width:4px;height:4px;border-radius:50%;background:#e2231a"></span>05 / Services
    </div>
    <div data-draw style="height:1px;background:rgba(13,13,13,.26)"></div>
    <div data-r="g2" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:0 56px;padding-top:20px">
      {
        services.map((sv) => (
          <div
            style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;align-items:baseline;gap:16px;padding:17px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(13,13,13,.1)"
            data-rv
          >
            <span style="display:block;width:16px;height:1px;background:#e2231a" />
            <span style="font-size:13px;line-height:1.7;opacity:.75">{sv}</span>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding:120px var(--gut) 0">
    <div data-r="g12" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(12,1fr);gap:28px;align-items:end">
      {/*
        The "Working with us" label and its paragraph are removed at the practice's
        request. The Start a project link stays and keeps its own column, so it sits
        where it always did rather than sliding left into the empty half.
      */}
      <div style="grid-column:8 / span 5;text-align:right" data-rv>
        <a
          class="wva-ghost-cta"
          href="/contact"
          style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;border:1px solid rgba(13,13,13,.26);padding:13px 22px;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.22em;text-transform:uppercase;white-space:nowrap;transition:background-color .5s ease,color .5s ease,border-color .5s ease"
          >Start a project <span style="color:#e2231a">↗</span></a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style is:global>
  /* Page-specific overrides carried across verbatim from WVA Studio.dc.html. */
  @keyframes stUp {
    from {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(20px);
    }
    to {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: translateY(0);
    }
  }

  [data-rv] {
    transform: translateY(22px);
    transition:
      opacity 1.05s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1),
      transform 1.05s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
  }

  [data-mask] {
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  [data-mask] > img {
    transition:
      transform 1.7s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1),
      clip-path 1.4s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1),
      filter 0.8s ease;
  }

  figure[data-plate]:hover > [data-mask] > img {
    transform: scale(1.04);
    filter: contrast(1.05);
  }

  [data-cl]:hover {
    border-color: #0d0d0d;
    color: #0d0d0d;
  }

  /* `style-hover` in the export — a Claude Design attribute with no browser meaning. */
  .wva-ghost-cta:hover {
    background: #0d0d0d;
    color: #ffffff;
    border-color: #0d0d0d;
  }

  @media (max-width: 980px) {
    section[style*='186px'] {
      padding-top: 150px !important;
    }
    /*
     * [RESPONSIVE FIX] The shared rule for this grid sets `margin-top: 0 !important` on
     * every direct child when it collapses to one column, which is right for the blocks
     * it was written for but would run the Practice and Principal paragraphs together
     * into one wall of text. Spacing is restored between them, and after the name.
     */
    [data-prose] + [data-prose],
    h2 + [data-prose] {
      margin-top: 22px !important;
    }
    /* Two columns of credentials have nowhere to go on a narrow screen. */
    [data-r='credgrid'] {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr !important;
      margin-top: 28px !important;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    section[style*='186px'] {
      padding-top: 172px !important;
    }
    figure > div[style*='vh'],
    span[data-mask] {
      max-height: 44vh;
    }
  }
</style>
